    <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
      <body>
        <div rend="parallel">
            <p xml:id="Aink451-kilavi">vēntaṟku uṟṟuḻip pirinta talaimakaṉ kuṟitta paruvam niṉaintu āṟṟiyirunta talaimakaḷ apparuva varaviṉkaṇ pācaṟaiyiṉiṉṟum vantār aracaṉ ceyti kūṟak kēṭṭu āṟṟāḷāyc colliyatu.</p>
            <p xml:lang="en">Considering the season indicated by the hero who had separated for a royal emergency, the heroine who had endured it, having become unable to endure on hearing the news of the king told by those who had come from the warcamp at the coming of that season, spoke [this].</p>
              </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
          <lg xml:id="Aink451">        
            <l>kārcey kālaiyoṭu kaiyaṟap pirintōr</l>
            <l>tērtaru viruntiṟ ṟavirkutal yāvatu</l>
            <l>māṟṟarun tāṉai nōkki</l>
            <l>yāṟṟavu miruttal vēntaṉatu toḻilē.</l>
        </lg>  
 <lg xml:lang="en">                    
<l>Along with the season made by the rains, the one who left so I am desolate -</l>
<l>how is there desisting from [being] a guest brought on chariot?<note xml:lang="en" place="foot">The literal translation obscures the point of this line somwhat. As I understand it, the point of the heroine's speech is to say that the king has no choice to be on the fronlines of the battle - it is his ultimate duty -- but the hero, on the other hand, ought to be returning to her.</note></l>
<l>Regarding the army that is difficult to oppose,</l>
<l>staying [there] longer<note xml:lang="en" place="foot"><foreign xml:lang="ta-Latn">āṟṟavum</foreign> is an intensiying adverb, hence 'longer' in dureation to period of time.</note> is the task of the king.</l>

</lg>                      
        </div>
      </body>
    </text>
